  <data name="Slide1Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This is the work of thousands of people – rare, valuable albums – and I want to preserve them. All the albums on this site have been archived onto BDXL discs (100 GB) for my personal collection. The site only contains links to the original sources and Discogs (where possible).</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Slide2Label" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Technical information</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Slide2Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Storing digitisation information – hardware details (player, amplifier, etc.) and format details (audio format, sample rate). The ability to see the hardware configurations used to digitise a particular album, or conversely, to find all albums digitised using a specific set of equipment.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Slide3Label" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Comparison</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Slide3Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>High-quality equipment and rare albums can be quite expensive. Before buying equipment or an album, you can follow the links to the original source to listen to various releases that have been digitized using different set-ups, and get a rough idea of whether they’re right for you or not, so you can find the best option for yourself.</value>
